  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through next Friday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: Showers and thunderstorms continue \ntoday as an upper level trough swings north through the region. \nThe trough exit tomorrow will result in a much more stable \natmosphere, but weak storm potential does persist in far eastern \nNevada. Sunday through Tuesday are expected to be dry, with a slow\nwarming trend due to developing ridging over the West. This will \nresult in high temperatures just below normal for this time of \nyear, with highs in the upper 80s. While model agreement has \nincreased significantly for the first half of the week, the \nforecast for late week remains variable, with disagreement \nfocusing on the timing of a West Coast trough impact. The slower \nsolution would maintain warm and dry conditions through next \nweekend while the faster solution would bring cooler temperatures \nand storm potential as early as Thursday or Friday.\n\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: High confidence in weakening\nstorms today and tomorrow. Moderate confidence in dry weather and\nnear normal temperatures through Wednesday. Low confidence past\nWednesday. No changes from the NBM.",
